From 7bb21ed1e7b158507d1c11ea6d3a267891292343 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agent 2 - Second Pass Audit <agent2-debug@local>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 08:03:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(frontend): wire up admin routes and fix broken
 auth/image contracts

- Route /admin/login, /admin/dashboard, /admin/create, /admin/update/:id
  and a 404 catch-all in App.js. LoginPage, ViewListings, CreateListing,
  UpdateListing, and ProtectedRoute existed but were never mounted in
  the router, making the entire admin dashboard unreachable.
- Fix AuthContext/LoginPage contract mismatch: LoginPage was making its
  own login API call and then invoking login(user, token), while
  AuthContext.login expected (email, password) and performed its own
  API call internally. LoginPage now delegates to the existing
  login(email, password) contract (already used correctly by the
  header's login modal), so sign-in actually completes.
- Add isAuthenticated/isHost to AuthContext's exposed value.
  ProtectedRoute read these already, but they never existed on the
  context, so !isAuthenticated was always true and every protected
  route redirected to login regardless of real auth state.
- Fix image URLs on the public site (LocationCard, LocationDetailsPage):
  both hardcoded http://localhost:5000 and concatenated it directly
  against the bare filename with no /uploads/ segment or separator,
  producing malformed URLs in both dev and production. Added a
  BACKEND_URL export to utils/api.js (mirroring services/api.js) and
  used it consistently.
- Fix CI build failures: CRA promotes ESLint warnings to build errors
  under CI=true, which Render sets by default. Removed unused vars,
  added a scoped eslint-disable for decorative footer anchors, and
  annotated two intentional single-run useEffects. Verified with
  CI=true npx react-scripts build before and after.
